# Sky Transfers — legacy URL redirects: A RECORD, NOT A LIVE CONFIG FILE
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. Nothing in this file redirects anything.
# The site is hosted on Render, which does not read _redirects — it serves it
# as an ordinary static asset (GET /_redirects returns 200 with this text).
#
# The rules that actually run are entered in the Render dashboard under the
# sky-transfers-website service > Redirect/Rewrite Rules. Changing a line here
# changes nothing on the site; change it there, then update this file to match
# so the two do not drift.
#
# This file is kept because it is the readable record of all 65 rules and why
# each exists, which the dashboard has no room for.
#
# Format below:  <source> <destination> <status>
# Generated 2026-09-17 from a crawl of all 330 historical URLs on the domain.
# Verified against the live site 2026-09-19: all 65 rules return 301 to the
# destination shown.
#
# Rules are matched top to bottom, first match wins, so the exact paths come
# before any wildcard. Fragments (#book, #fleet) are stripped by browsers and
# ignored by crawlers — they are here only so a human landing on an old link
# arrives at the right part of the page.

